.TH WATCHMAN 1 "June 2026" "Watchman 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
watchman \- automated Git maintenance, rebasing, tagging, and repo health tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B watchman
[\fB--full\fR]
.br
.B watchman
\fB-r\fR \fIPATH\fR
.br
.B watchman
\fBstatus\fR
.br
.B watchman
\fBdoctor\fR
.br
.B watchman
\fBinit\fR \fIPATH\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Watchman is an automated Git maintenance utility designed to keep multiple
repositories clean, updated, and production-safe. It performs nightly commits,
rebases development branches onto the primary branch, and automatically tags
releases when merges occur.

Watchman is intended for environments where:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmain\fR is the production branch
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdev\fR is the working branch
.IP \(bu 2
automation must never modify production directly
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B --full
Runs a full scan of all configured repositories.
.TP
.B -r, --repo PATH
Runs Watchman on a single repository.
.TP
.B status
Displays configuration, scan paths, and general system information.
.TP
.B doctor
Runs health checks on Git, networking, permissions, and environment.
.TP
.B init PATH
Initializes a new repository with:
.IP \(bu 2
primary branch detection (main/master)
.IP \(bu 2
dev branch creation
.IP \(bu 2
initial commit if needed
.IP \(bu 2
remote setup (optional)
.SH FILES
.TP
/var/log/nightly-commit-YYYY-MM-DD.log
Daily log file generated by Watchman.
.SH AUTHOR
Zach Daniels <github.com/Cazgem>
.SH SEE ALSO
git(1), systemd(1)
